{"catalogue_version":"2026.09.16","hits":[{"doc_url":"/docs/nhcx/v1/getting-started/get-your-sandbox-credentials","id":"nhcx.sandbox.prerequisites","summary":"The checklist to complete before your system can register on the claims exchange sandbox: a facility registration, sandbox credentials, basic health ID featu...","title":"What you need before you register on the NHCX sandbox","type":"sandbox"},{"doc_url":"","id":"nhcx.test.provider-uc-01","summary":"Prove that your hospital system can fetch the registered participants of one role, such as every payer, from the claims exchange.","title":"Provider sandbox exit use case 1: Get participant list","type":"test"},{"doc_url":"/docs/nhcx/v1/getting-started/get-your-sandbox-credentials","id":"nhcx.flow.sandbox-onboarding","summary":"Register your system in the claims exchange test environment so it holds a participant code, a registered certificate and a callback address.","title":"Onboard as a participant in the NHCX sandbox","type":"flow"},{"doc_url":"","id":"nhcx.callback.notification-delivery","summary":"What a patient app receives when the claims exchange pushes a claim update for a patient who logged in to it, and how to handle it.","title":"Receiving a notification on a patient app","type":"callback"},{"doc_url":"/docs/nhcx/v1/reference/notifications-and-patient-apps#subscribing","id":"nhcx.flow.notification-subscribe","summary":"Have a patient's health record app receive plain-language updates on their pre-authorisations, claims and payments, by subscribing each time the patient logs...","title":"Subscribe a patient app to notifications","type":"flow"},{"doc_url":"/docs/nhcx/v1/getting-started/receiving-a-callback","id":"nhcx.sandbox.callback-url-requirements","summary":"What the web address that receives exchange messages must look like, the three addresses the exchange sends from, and how fast your server must answer.","title":"Callback URL rules and the egress addresses to allow","type":"sandbox"},{"doc_url":