{"catalogue_version":"2026.09.16","hits":[{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/getting-started/glossary#hie-cm","id":"shared.glossary.hie-cm","summary":"The ABDM building block that holds ABHA addresses, the links to each address's records, and the consent that authorises sharing them. It is not the gateway.","title":"HIE-CM, Health Information Exchange and Consent Manager","type":"glossary"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/getting-started/glossary#gateway","id":"shared.glossary.gateway","summary":"The component that routes calls between participants so they never call each other directly. It is not the consent manager, and no health record passes throu...","title":"Gateway, the routing layer between participants","type":"glossary"},{"doc_url":"/docs/nhcx/v1/getting-started/fetching-a-recipient-certificate#what-comes-back","id":"hiecm.glossary.key-material","summary":"The ECDH key pairs that encrypt health records in transit. A fresh pair per transfer, the HIU keeps its own, and the HIP returns its public half alongside th...","title":"Key material, who generates it and who keeps it","type":"glossary"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/api/m3/endpoints/m3-callbacks/02-m3-post-v3-hiu-consent-request-on-status#m3-on-consent-request-status","id":"hiecm.callback.m3-on-consent-request-status","summary":"ABDM answers a consent status request on the HIU's bridge with the request's current state.","title":"The consent manager reports the state of a consent request you asked about","type":"callback"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/getting-started/build-it-well#read-the-error-then-decide-error-codes","id":"hiecm.glossary.x-cm-id","summary":"The header naming which consent manager a request is meant for, carrying that consent manager's suffix.","title":"X-CM-ID, the consent manager header","type":"glossary"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/getting-started/glossary#consent-manager","id":"hiecm.glossary.consent-manager","summary":"The component that receives consent requests, shows them to the patient, and records the decision.","title":"Consent manager, the component that holds consent","type":"glossary"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/api/m2/errors#abdm-2403","id":"hiecm.error.abdm-2403","summary":"The consent manager header does not match the environment you are calling.","title":"ABDM-2403, the X-CM-ID is not valid","type":"error"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/concepts/how-it-fits#roles","id":"hiecm.concept.roles","summary":"Your role, IMS or PHR, is fixed by the entity your software acts for, while HIP and HIU change with the direction each record moves.","title":"Roles, which entity your software acts for and which way the record moves","type":"concept"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/concepts/consent#consent-in-a-phr-app","id":"hiecm.concept.consent-in-a-phr-app","summary":"A personal health record app must let a person see a consent request, change it, allow or refuse it, see what is allowed, and take it back.","title":"The five things a personal health record application must let a person do with consent","type":"concept"},{"doc_url":"","id":"nhcx.concept.beneficiary-consent","summary":"The patient's data stays sealed from the exchange, research sees only aggregates, individual data needs the patient's consent, and the patient must agree bef...","title":"Beneficiary consent and data rights","type":"concept"}]}
